var e={"p ← the address of x":`p ← x 的地址`,"read the value at p        // 42":`讀取 p 處的值        // 42`,"the value at p ← 7         // x is now 7":`p 處的值 ← 7         // x 現在是 7`,"p ← nothing":`p ← 空`,"Who holds what":`誰存著什麼`,"Numbered cells":`帶編號的格子`,"A computer’s memory is one long row of cells. Every cell has a number, its <strong>address</strong>, and can hold one value.":`計算機的記憶體是一長排格子。每個格子都有一個編號，即它的<strong>地址</strong>，並且能存放一個值。`,"Here are seven of them, at addresses 100 to 106. Real memory has billions.":`這裡有七個，地址從 100 到 106。真實的記憶體有幾十億個。`,"A street of houses. The address tells you where; the house holds what.":`一條街上的房子。地址告訴你在哪裡，房子裡放著東西。`,"Nothing is stored yet.":`還什麼都沒存。`,"A variable is a named cell":`變數是有名字的格子`,Store:`儲存`,"Writing <strong>x ← 42</strong> picks a free cell, puts 42 in it, and remembers that <em>x</em> means that cell.":`寫下 <strong>x ← 42</strong>，就會選一個空閒的格子，把 42 放進去，並記住 <em>x</em> 指的就是這個格子。`,"You say x; the computer goes to address 102.":`你說 x，計算機就去地址 102。`,"The name is for you. The machine only ever uses the address.":`名字是給你看的。機器只用地址。`,"at 102":`在 102`,"A pointer holds an address":`指標存放地址`,Point:`指向`,"A cell can hold any number, and an address is a number. So a cell can hold the address of another cell.":`一個格子可以存放任何數字，而地址也是數字。所以一個格子可以存放另一個格子的地址。`,"That is a <strong>pointer</strong>. Here <em>p</em> lives at 105 and holds 102: it points at x.":`這就是<strong>指標</strong>。這裡 <em>p</em> 位於 105，存放著 102：它指向 x。`,"“p knows where x is,” not “p is 42.”":`是「p 知道 x 在哪裡」，而不是「p 是 42」。`,"at 105":`在 105`,"Follow the pointer":`沿著指標走`,"To use a pointer you <strong>follow</strong> it: read the address it holds, go to that cell, and take what is there.":`要使用指標，就要<strong>沿著</strong>它走：讀出它存放的地址，去那個格子，取出那裡的東西。`,"Following p leads to cell 102, which holds 42.":`沿著 p 走就到了格子 102，裡面存著 42。`,"One extra hop. This is the hop a linked list makes for every node.":`多跳了一次。連結串列的每個節點都要這樣跳一次。`,"value at p → 42":`p 處的值 → 42`,"Write through it":`透過它寫入`,Write:`寫入`,"You can also store through a pointer. Putting 7 “at p” goes to cell 102 and replaces what is there.":`你也可以透過指標存值。把 7 放到「p 處」，就會去格子 102，替換掉那裡的內容。`,"Nobody mentioned x, but x is now 7. It is the same cell.":`沒人提到 x，但 x 現在是 7 了。因為是同一個格子。`,"This is how one part of a program changes data another part thought was its own.":`程式的一部分就是這樣改掉了另一部分以為屬於自己的資料。`,"x is now 7":`x 現在是 7`,"Two pointers, one cell":`兩個指標，一個格子`,Copy:`複製`,"Copying a pointer copies the <em>address</em>, not the thing it points at. <strong>q ← p</strong> gives q the number 102 too.":`複製指標複製的是<em>地址</em>，而不是它指向的東西。<strong>q ← p</strong> 讓 q 也得到數字 102。`,"Now p and q both lead to the same cell. Change it through either and both see the change.":`現在 p 和 q 都通向同一個格子。透過任何一個修改它，兩個都能看到變化。`,"at 100":`在 100`,"Pointing at nothing":`什麼都不指向`,"A pointer does not have to point anywhere. A special value, usually called <strong>null</strong>, means “nothing”.":`指標不一定要指向某處。有一個特殊的值，通常叫 <strong>null</strong>，意思是「什麼都沒有」。`,"p is now null. q still points at x, and x is untouched.":`p 現在是 null。q 仍然指向 x，x 沒有被動過。`,"Following a null pointer is an error. It is what ends a linked list.":`沿著空指標走是一個錯誤。連結串列的結尾就是它。`},t={"if n = 1:":`如果 n = 1:`,"return 1              // base case":`返回 1              // 基本情況`,"return n × fact(n − 1)    // smaller copy":`返回 n × fact(n − 1)    // 更小的副本`,"Who is waiting":`誰在等待`,"A function that calls itself":`呼叫自己的函式`,"The factorial of 4 is 4 × 3 × 2 × 1. But 3 × 2 × 1 is the factorial of 3, so <strong>fact(4) = 4 × fact(3)</strong>: the problem contains a smaller copy of itself.":`4 的階乘是 4 × 3 × 2 × 1。但 3 × 2 × 1 是 3 的階乘，所以 <strong>fact(4) = 4 × fact(3)</strong>：問題裡包含著一個更小的自己。`,"A function written that way is <strong>recursive</strong>. Calling it puts a <em>frame</em> on the call stack: its notes while it runs.":`這樣寫的函式是<strong>遞迴</strong>的。呼叫它會在呼叫堆疊上放一個<em>堆積疊框</em>：它執行時的筆記。`,"Asking a question whose answer needs the same question, about something smaller.":`提一個問題，而它的答案需要對更小的東西提同一個問題。`,"needs fact(3)":`需要 fact(3)`,Running:`執行中`,nobody:`無`,"Frames on the stack":`堆疊上的堆積疊框`,"Calls pile up":`呼叫越疊越高`,Call:`呼叫`,"fact(4) cannot finish until it knows fact(3), so it calls it and waits. fact(3) needs fact(2), which needs fact(1).":`fact(4) 要知道 fact(3) 才能完成，所以它呼叫 fact(3) 並等待。fact(3) 需要 fact(2)，fact(2) 又需要 fact(1)。`,"Every call adds a frame on top. Nothing has been multiplied yet: the stack is only remembering who is waiting for whom.":`每次呼叫都在頂上加一個堆積疊框。還什麼都沒乘：堆疊只是記著誰在等誰。`,"needs fact(2)":`需要 fact(2)`,"needs fact(1)":`需要 fact(1)`,"The base case":`基本情況`,"fact(1) is different. It does not need another call: the answer is simply 1.":`fact(1) 不一樣。它不需要再呼叫別的：答案就是 1。`,"This is the <strong>base case</strong>, an input small enough to answer directly. It is where the pile stops growing.":`這就是<strong>基本情況</strong>：一個小到可以直接回答的輸入。堆疊就是在這裡停止增長的。`,"Every recursion needs a base case, and every call must move towards it.":`每個遞迴都需要基本情況，而且每次呼叫都必須朝它靠近。`,"returns 1":`返回 1`,"Handing the answer back":`把答案交回去`,Return:`返回`,"fact(1) returns 1 and its frame comes off the stack. That 1 is exactly what fact(2) was waiting for.":`fact(1) 返回 1，它的堆積疊框從堆疊上移除。這個 1 正是 fact(2) 在等的。`,"Now fact(2) can do its own small job: 2 × 1 = 2.":`現在 fact(2) 可以做自己的小工作了：2 × 1 = 2。`,Unwinding:`展開`,"The same thing happens one frame down. fact(2) returns 2, and fact(3) finishes: 3 × 2 = 6.":`往下一幀也是同樣的過程。fact(2) 返回 2，fact(3) 完成：3 × 2 = 6。`,"The calls went up the stack; the answers come back down it, in the opposite order.":`呼叫沿著堆疊往上走；答案按相反的順序沿著堆疊往下回來。`,"Last called, first finished. The call stack is a stack.":`最後呼叫的，最先完成。呼叫堆疊就是一個堆疊。`,"The answer":`答案`,"fact(3) returns 6 to the first call, which has been waiting all this time: 4 × 6 = <strong>24</strong>.":`fact(3) 把 6 返回給第一次呼叫，它一直在等：4 × 6 = <strong>24</strong>。`,"Four calls, four frames. Recursion uses memory in proportion to how deep it goes.":`四次呼叫，四個堆積疊框。遞迴佔用的記憶體與它的深度成正比。`,"Without a base case":`沒有基本情況`,"Take the base case away and fact(1) calls fact(0), which calls fact(−1), and on, and on. No call ever returns.":`去掉基本情況，fact(1) 就會呼叫 fact(0)，fact(0) 又呼叫 fact(−1)，沒完沒了。沒有一次呼叫會返回。`,"Each one still needs a frame, and the stack has only so much room. When it runs out, the program stops: a <strong>stack overflow</strong>.":`每次呼叫仍然需要一個堆積疊框，而堆疊的空間是有限的。空間用完時，程式就會停止：這就是<strong>堆疊溢位</strong>。`,"Deep recursion can overflow even with a base case. A loop uses one frame, however long it runs.":`即使有基本情況，太深的遞迴也會溢位。迴圈無論執行多久，都只用一個堆積疊框。`,"stack overflow":`堆疊溢位`,"More frames than the stack has room for.":`堆積疊框多到堆疊裝不下。`},n={"return a[i]":`返回 a[i]`,"for each item from the last down to i:":`對每個 項，從最後一項到第 i 項:`,"move it one cell right":`把它右移一格`,"for each item after i, from left to right:":`對每個 i 之後的項，從左到右:`,"move it one cell left":`把它左移一格`,"put x in the first free cell":`把 x 放進第一個空格子`,"Cells in a row":`一排格子`,"An array is one block of memory cut into equal cells, numbered from 0. The values sit side by side, in order, with no gaps.":`陣列是一整塊記憶體，切成大小相同的格子，從 0 開始編號。值一個挨一個按順序排著，中間沒有空隙。`,"This one has room for seven values and is holding five. Call it <strong>a</strong>.":`這個陣列能放七個值，現在放了五個。叫它 <strong>a</strong>。`,"A row of numbered lockers, all the same size.":`一排帶編號的儲物櫃，大小都一樣。`,"Jump straight there":`直接跳過去`,"Because every cell is the same size, the computer can work out where cell 3 is: the start of the array, plus three cells along.":`因為每個格子大小相同，計算機可以算出格子 3 在哪裡：陣列的起點，再往後數三個格子。`,"So it goes straight there. It does not visit cells 0, 1 and 2 on the way, however long the array is.":`所以它直接跳過去。不管陣列多長，它都不會順路經過格子 0、1 和 2。`,"O(1). A linked list would have to hop there node by node.":`O(1)。連結串列就得一個節點一個節點地跳過去。`,"To put 15 at index 2, cell 2 has to be empty first. So 31, 25 and 19 each move one cell to the right, starting from the end.":`要把 15 放到索引 2，格子 2 必須先空出來。所以 31、25 和 19 從末尾開始，各自右移一格。`,"Only then can 15 go in.":`然後 15 才能放進去。`,"O(n): the nearer the front you insert, the more there is to move.":`O(n)：插入的位置越靠前，要移動的就越多。`,"Taking 12 out leaves a hole at index 1, and an array may not have holes.":`拿掉 12 會在索引 1 留下一個洞，而陣列不能有洞。`,"So everything after it moves one cell to the left to close the gap.":`所以它後面的所有值都左移一格，把空隙填上。`,"O(n) again: four values moved to remove one.":`又是 O(n)：為了刪一個值，移動了四個。`,"Adding at the end is the cheap case. 40 goes into the first free cell, and nothing else has to move.":`在末尾新增是便宜的情況。40 放進第一個空格子，其他什麼都不用動。`,"O(1), as long as there is a free cell.":`O(1)，只要還有空格子。`,"When it is full":`滿了怎麼辦`,"Add 52 and every cell is used. An array cannot grow where it stands: the memory just past it belongs to something else.":`再加 52，所有格子就都用上了。陣列不能原地變大：緊挨著它的記憶體屬於別的東西。`,"To hold more you need a bigger array, and to copy everything across. A dynamic array does that for you.":`要放更多，你需要一個更大的陣列，並把所有東西複製過去。動態陣列會替你做這件事。`,"Lots of “give me item i”: array. Lots of inserting in the middle: linked list.":`經常「給我第 i 項」：用陣列。經常在中間插入：用連結串列。`},r={"table ← for each beginning of pattern, the length of":`table ← 對模式的每個開頭部分，記下`,"its longest start, short of the whole, that is also its end":`它最長的、不是整體的、同時也是結尾的開頭的長度`,"m ← 0                          // letters matched so far":`m ← 0                          // 已匹配的字母數`,"for each letter c of text:":`對每個 文字中的字母 c:`,"while m > 0 and c ≠ pattern[m]:":`當 m > 0 且 c ≠ pattern[m]:`,"m ← table[m − 1]       // fall back, re-read nothing":`m ← table[m − 1]       // 回退，不重讀任何東西`,"if c = pattern[m]: m ← m + 1":`如果 c = pattern[m]: m ← m + 1`,"if m = length of pattern: return found":`如果 m = 模式的長度: 返回 找到`,"Never look twice":`永不看兩遍`,"The simple search found A B A C in this text with nine comparisons. Each time it failed it moved along one place and started the pattern again from its first letter, re-reading text it had already seen.":`簡單的搜尋用了九次比較，才在這段文字裡找到 A B A C。每次失敗，它都右移一位，再從第一個字母重新開始模式，重讀已經看過的文字。`,"The <strong>Knuth–Morris–Pratt</strong> search, KMP, reads each letter of the text once and never goes back.":`<strong>Knuth–Morris–Pratt</strong> 搜尋，即 KMP，文字的每個字母只讀一次，從不回頭。`,"Fallback table":`回退表`,"for A, AB, ABA, ABAC":`對應 A、AB、ABA、ABAC`,"Three match, then a miss":`三個匹配，然後失配`,"It begins the same way. A, B, A all match. The fourth letter does not: the pattern wants C and the text has B.":`開頭一樣。A、B、A 都匹配。第四個字母不匹配：模式要 C，文字是 B。`,"The simple search would now throw those three matches away.":`簡單的搜尋這時會把這三個匹配全扔掉。`,"What the matches already say":`匹配已經告訴了你什麼`,"Three letters matched, so the text there is known to be A B A, without looking at it again. Could a match start one place along? It would need B to equal A. No.":`三個字母匹配了，所以不用再看就知道那裡的文字是 A B A。匹配能從後一位開始嗎？那需要 B 等於 A。不行。`,"Two places along? It would need A to equal A. Yes. That works because the matched part <strong>ends the way it begins</strong>: with an A.":`後兩位呢？那需要 A 等於 A。可以。之所以可行，是因為匹配的部分<strong>結尾和開頭一樣</strong>：都是 A。`,"starts and ends with A":`以 A 開頭，也以 A 結尾`,"ABA: its longest start that is also its end has length 1.":`ABA：既是開頭又是結尾的最長部分，長度為 1。`,"Slide so they line up":`滑動到對齊`,"So slide the pattern two places, putting its first A under the A that ended the match. That letter is already known to match. It is not compared again.":`所以把模式滑兩位，讓它的第一個 A 對準結束匹配的那個 A。已知那個字母是匹配的，不再比較。`,"One of the pattern’s letters is accounted for before a single new comparison is made.":`還沒做一次新的比較，模式就有一個字母已經確定了。`,"known: no need to look":`已知：不用看`,"Carry on from where the text stopped":`從文字停下的地方繼續`,"The text was at its fourth letter, and it stays there. Compare it with the pattern’s second letter: B = B. Then A = A, then C = C.":`文字停在第四個字母，現在也還在那裡。把它和模式的第二個字母比較：B = B。然後 A = A，然後 C = C。`,"Found at place 2 with seven comparisons instead of nine, and no letter of the text read twice.":`在位置 2 找到，七次比較而不是九次，文字中沒有一個字母讀了兩遍。`,"The table that makes it work":`讓它運轉的那張表`,"How far to fall back depends only on the pattern, so it is worked out once, before the search. For every beginning of the pattern, note the length of its longest start that is also its end: A is 0, AB is 0, ABA is 1, ABAC is 0.":`回退多遠只取決於模式，所以在搜尋之前算一次就行。對模式的每個開頭部分，記下它既是開頭又是結尾的最長部分的長度：A 是 0，AB 是 0，ABA 是 1，ABAC 是 0。`,"After a miss with m letters matched, keep table[m − 1] of them and carry on.":`匹配了 m 個字母後失配，就保留其中 table[m − 1] 個，繼續往下。`,"O(n + m) for a text of n letters and a pattern of m. The simple search is O(n × m) at worst.":`文字 n 個字母、模式 m 個字母時是 O(n + m)。簡單的搜尋最壞是 O(n × m)。`},i={"Finding a cell":`找一個格子`,"Rows and columns":`行與列`,"An array has one index. A <strong>matrix</strong>, or 2D array, has two: a row and a column. Images, game boards, spreadsheets and maps are all stored this way.":`陣列有一個索引。<strong>矩陣</strong>，也就是二維陣列，有兩個：行和列。圖片、棋盤、電子表格和地圖都是這樣儲存的。`,"This one has 3 rows and 4 columns: twelve cells.":`這個矩陣有 3 行 4 列：十二個格子。`,"3 rows × 4 columns":`3 行 × 4 列`,Cell:`格子`,"Place in memory":`在記憶體中的位置`,"row × 4 + column":`行 × 4 + 列`,"Two numbers find a cell":`兩個數確定一個格子`,Access:`訪問`,"Give a row and a column and you have the cell: row 1, column 2. As with a plain array, nothing is searched. It is still O(1).":`給出行和列，就得到了格子：第 1 行，第 2 列。和普通陣列一樣，不需要搜尋。仍然是 O(1)。`,"row 1, column 2":`第 1 行，第 2 列`,"Really one long row":`其實是一長排`,"Memory has no second dimension. The rows are simply laid end to end: row 0, then row 1, then row 2.":`記憶體沒有第二個維度。各行只是首尾相接地排著：第 0 行，然後第 1 行，然後第 2 行。`,"So a cell’s real position is <strong>row × width + column</strong>. Row 1, column 2 is at 1 × 4 + 2 = 6, which is the number written on it.":`所以一個格子真正的位置是<strong>行 × 寬度 + 列</strong>。第 1 行第 2 列位於 1 × 4 + 2 = 6，正是寫在它上面的數字。`,"row 1 is 4 to 7":`第 1 行是 4 到 7`,"The number in each cell is its place in memory.":`每個格子裡的數字是它在記憶體中的位置。`,"Which way you walk matters":`走的方向很重要`,"Walking along a row visits cells that sit side by side in memory. Walking down a column jumps four places each time.":`沿著一行走，訪問的格子在記憶體中是挨著的。沿著一列往下走，每次都要跳四個位置。`,"Both visit every cell, but on a large matrix the row-by-row walk can be several times faster, because computers read memory in neighbouring chunks.":`兩種走法都會訪問每個格子，但在大矩陣上，一行一行地走可能快好幾倍，因為計算機是一塊一塊地讀取相鄰記憶體的。`,"Loop over rows on the outside, columns on the inside.":`外層迴圈遍歷行，內層迴圈遍歷列。`,"every fourth cell":`每隔四個格子`,"column 2":`第 2 列`,"A cell’s neighbours are one step away in each direction: up, down, left, right. Add or subtract 1 from the row or the column.":`一個格子的鄰居在每個方向上都只差一步：上、下、左、右。把行或列加 1 或減 1 即可。`,"That turns a grid into a graph without storing a single edge, which is how mazes, flood fills and many dynamic-programming tables are handled.":`這樣不用存一條邊，就把網格變成了圖，迷宮、泛洪填充和許多動態規劃表格都是這樣處理的。`,"four neighbours":`四個鄰居`,"Check the edges: corner cells have only two.":`注意邊緣：角上的格子只有兩個鄰居。`},a={"put x on top":`把 x 放到頂上`,"if the stack is empty: error":`如果 堆疊為空: 錯誤`,"take the top item off":`把頂上的項拿走`,"return the top item, leaving it there":`返回 頂上的項，並把它留在原處`,"return whether nothing is left":`返回 是否什麼都沒剩下`,"What is a stack?":`堆疊是什麼？`,"A stack is a pile. You can add to the top and take from the top, and that is all.":`堆疊就是一摞東西。你只能往頂上放，從頂上拿，僅此而已。`,"So the last item you put on is the first one you get back: <strong>LIFO</strong>, last in, first out.":`所以你最後放上去的，就是你最先拿回來的：<strong>LIFO</strong>，後進先出。`,"A pile of plates. Nobody pulls one out from the middle.":`一摞盤子。沒人會從中間抽出一個。`,"<strong>push(x)</strong> puts a new item on top. Here 40 leaves the input tray and lands on the pile.":`<strong>push(x)</strong> 把一個新項放到頂上。這裡 40 離開輸入托盤，落到這一摞上。`,"Nothing underneath has to move, so a push costs the same whether the stack holds three items or three million.":`下面的東西都不用動，所以不管堆疊裡有三個項還是三百萬個，一次 push 的代價都一樣。`,"O(1): one step, however tall the stack is.":`O(1)：一步，不管堆疊有多高。`,Top:`堆疊頂`,"<strong>top()</strong> tells you what is on top without taking it off. You will also see it called <em>peek</em>.":`<strong>top()</strong> 告訴你頂上是什麼，但不把它拿走。你也會看到它叫 <em>peek</em>。`,"The stack is exactly as it was afterwards.":`之後堆疊和原來一模一樣。`,"O(1): the top is always in the same place.":`O(1)：堆疊頂總在同一個地方。`,"<strong>pop()</strong> removes the top item and hands it back. It is the only way to take anything out of a stack.":`<strong>pop()</strong> 拿走頂上的項並把它交給你。這是從堆疊裡取出東西的唯一方法。`,"40 was the last block in, so it is the first one out.":`40 是最後放進去的方塊，所以它最先出來。`,"Popping an empty stack is an error. Check empty() first.":`對空堆疊執行 pop 是一個錯誤。先檢查 empty()。`,"Last in, first out":`後進先出`,"Pop again and 30 comes out. The blocks went in as 10, 20, 30, 40 and they are leaving as 40, 30, …":`再 pop 一次，30 出來了。方塊按 10、20、30、40 進去，現在按 40、30、…… 出來。`,"A stack always gives things back in the reverse of the order they arrived.":`堆疊總是按到達順序的相反順序把東西還給你。`,"To reach 10 at the bottom, everything above it has to come off first.":`要拿到底部的 10，上面的所有東西都得先拿走。`,"Each time a function calls another, the computer pushes a frame onto the <strong>call stack</strong>. When the function returns, its frame is popped and the caller carries on.":`每當一個函式呼叫另一個函式，計算機就往<strong>呼叫堆疊</strong>上壓入一個堆積疊框。函式返回時，它的堆積疊框被彈出，呼叫者繼續執行。`,"Undo history and the browser’s Back button work the same way.":`撤銷歷史和瀏覽器的「後退」按鈕也是這樣工作的。`,"“Stack overflow” is this stack running out of room, usually from recursion that never stops.":`「堆疊溢位」就是這個堆疊空間用完了，通常是因為遞迴停不下來。`},o={"put x at the rear":`把 x 放到隊尾`,"if the queue is empty: error":`如果 佇列為空: 錯誤`,"take the front item off":`把隊首的項拿走`,"return the front item, leaving it there":`返回 隊首的項，並把它留在原處`,"What is a queue?":`佇列是什麼？`,"A queue is a line. You join at the back and you leave from the front, and nobody jumps ahead.":`佇列就是排隊。你從隊尾加入，從隊首離開，誰也不能插隊。`,"So the first item in is the first one out: <strong>FIFO</strong>, first in, first out.":`所以最先進去的就是最先出來的：<strong>FIFO</strong>，先進先出。`,"The line at a checkout. Whoever has waited longest is served next.":`收銀臺前的隊伍。等得最久的人下一個被服務。`,"<strong>enqueue(x)</strong> adds a new item at the <strong>rear</strong>. Here 40 leaves the input tray and joins the back of the line.":`<strong>enqueue(x)</strong> 在<strong>隊尾</strong>加入一個新項。這裡 40 離開輸入托盤，排到了隊伍末尾。`,"Nobody already waiting has to move.":`已經在等的人都不用動。`,"O(1): one step, however long the line is.":`O(1)：一步，不管隊伍有多長。`,Front:`隊首`,"<strong>front()</strong> tells you who is next without taking them out of the line. You will also see it called <em>peek</em>.":`<strong>front()</strong> 告訴你下一個是誰，但不把它從隊伍裡拿出來。你也會看到它叫 <em>peek</em>。`,"The queue is exactly as it was afterwards.":`之後佇列和原來一模一樣。`,"O(1): the front is always in the same place.":`O(1)：隊首總在同一個地方。`,"<strong>dequeue()</strong> removes the item at the <strong>front</strong> and hands it back. 10 has waited longest, so 10 goes.":`<strong>dequeue()</strong> 移除<strong>隊首</strong>的項並把它交給你。10 等得最久，所以 10 離開。`,"Everyone behind moves up one place, and 20 is now at the front.":`後面的每個人都往前挪一位，現在 20 在隊首。`,"Dequeuing from an empty queue is an error.":`對空佇列執行 dequeue 是一個錯誤。`,"First in, first out":`先進先出`,"Dequeue again and 20 comes out. They joined as 10, 20, 30, 40 and they are leaving as 10, 20, …":`再 dequeue 一次，20 出來了。它們按 10、20、30、40 加入，現在按 10、20、…… 離開。`,"A queue gives things back in exactly the order they arrived. A stack gives them back in reverse.":`佇列按到達的順序原樣把東西還給你。堆疊則是倒過來還。`,"You add at one end and remove at the other. A stack does both at the same end.":`你在一端新增，在另一端移除。堆疊兩件事都在同一端做。`,"Whenever work arrives faster than it can be done, it waits in a queue. Send three files to a printer and they come out in the order you sent them.":`只要工作來得比做得快，它就會在佇列裡等著。給印表機發三個檔案，它們會按你傳送的順序列印出來。`,"Requests to a web server, keys you have typed, messages between programs: all queued.":`發往網頁伺服器的請求、你敲下的按鍵、程式之間的訊息：全都在排隊。`,"Exploring a maze level by level, or a graph breadth-first, also runs on a queue.":`一層一層地探索迷宮，或者廣度優先地遍歷圖，也都靠佇列。`},s={"put x at the front":`把 x 放到前端`,"put x at the back":`把 x 放到後端`,"take the front item off, return it":`把前端的項拿走並返回它`,"take the back item off, return it":`把後端的項拿走並返回它`,"put every letter in a deque":`把每個字母放進一個雙端佇列`,"while more than one is left:":`當 剩下的不止一個:`,"if pop_front() ≠ pop_back(): return no":`如果 pop_front() ≠ pop_back(): 返回 否`,"return yes":`返回 是`,"Open at both ends":`兩端都開口`,"A stack lets you in and out at one end. A queue lets you in at one end and out at the other. A <strong>deque</strong> (say “deck”) is a double-ended queue: you can add or remove at <em>either</em> end.":`堆疊讓你在一端進出。佇列讓你從一端進、從另一端出。<strong>雙端佇列</strong>（deque）是兩頭都能用的佇列：你可以在<em>任意一端</em>新增或移除。`,"It has a front and a back, and a way in and out at each.":`它有前端和後端，每一端都可以進出。`,"A train: carriages can be coupled or uncoupled at either end, never in the middle.":`一列火車：車廂可以在任意一端掛上或摘下，從不在中間。`,"Nothing in the middle is ever touched.":`中間的東西從來不會被碰到。`,"<strong>push_back(10)</strong> adds at the back. 10 becomes the new back; nothing else moves.":`<strong>push_back(10)</strong> 在後端新增。10 成為新的後端；其他什麼都不動。`,"So far this is just a queue’s enqueue.":`到目前為止，這只是佇列的入隊。`,"<strong>push_front(50)</strong> adds at the other end, in front of everything.":`<strong>push_front(50)</strong> 在另一端新增，排在所有東西前面。`,"A queue cannot do this: nobody is allowed to join at the front of a line.":`佇列做不到這一點：誰都不許插到隊伍最前面。`,"<strong>pop_front()</strong> takes the front item off and hands it back.":`<strong>pop_front()</strong> 把前端的項拿走並交給你。`,"50 went in at the front and came straight back out of it. Use only this end and a deque behaves as a <strong>stack</strong>.":`50 從前端進去，又直接從前端出來。只用這一端的話，雙端佇列就像一個<strong>堆疊</strong>。`,"In and out at one end: last in, first out.":`在同一端進出：後進先出。`,"<strong>pop_back()</strong> takes from the back instead.":`<strong>pop_back()</strong> 則從後端取。`,"Push at one end and pop at the other and it is a <strong>queue</strong>. A deque is both, and every one of its four operations is O(1).":`在一端壓入、在另一端彈出，它就是一個<strong>佇列</strong>。雙端佇列兩者兼備，而且四種操作都是 O(1)。`,"Only the ends change, so the length of the deque never matters.":`只有兩端會變，所以雙端佇列有多長都無所謂。`,"In at one end, out at the other: first in, first out.":`一端進，另一端出：先進先出。`,"Using both ends":`兩端一起用`,Example:`例子`,"Some jobs need both ends at once. Is LEVEL a <strong>palindrome</strong>, a word that reads the same backwards?":`有些工作需要同時用兩端。LEVEL 是<strong>迴文</strong>嗎？也就是倒著讀也一樣的詞？`,"Put its letters in a deque. If it is one, the letter at the front must always match the letter at the back.":`把它的字母放進雙端佇列。如果它是迴文，前端的字母必須總是和後端的字母一樣。`,"From the front":`從前端`,"From the back":`從後端`,"Letters left":`剩下的字母`,"Compare the ends":`比較兩端`,"Pop one letter from each end and compare them. L and L: they match, so carry on with what is left.":`從兩端各彈出一個字母，比較它們。L 和 L：一樣，所以繼續處理剩下的。`,"Neither pop had to search for anything. Each took one step.":`兩次彈出都不需要搜尋。每次只用一步。`,"They match.":`一樣。`,"Until one is left":`直到只剩一個`,"Again: E and E. They match too. One letter is left, and a single letter has nothing to disagree with.":`再來：E 和 E。也一樣。只剩一個字母，單個字母沒有什麼可以不一樣的。`,"LEVEL is a palindrome, found by working inwards from both ends.":`LEVEL 是迴文，這是從兩端往中間推算出來的。`,"Undo histories with a size limit, sliding-window maximums, schedulers that take work from either end.":`有長度上限的撤銷歷史、滑動視窗最大值、從任意一端取任務的排程器。`,"LEVEL is a palindrome.":`LEVEL 是迴文。`},c={"big-o":{"return a[0]":`返回 a[0]`,"repeat: look at the middle, keep one half":`重複: 看中間，留下一半`,"for each item in a:":`對每個 a 中的項:`,"add it on":`把它加上`,"for each other item in a:":`對每個 a 中的其他項:`,"compare the two":`比較這兩項`,"Steps taken":`所用步數`,"Count steps, not seconds":`數步數，不數秒數`,"How fast is an algorithm? Seconds depend on the machine. So instead we count <strong>steps</strong>, and ask how that count depends on the size of the input, <em>n</em>.":`一個演算法有多快？秒數取決於機器。所以我們改為數<strong>步數</strong>，並且問：這個數字如何隨輸入規模 <em>n</em> 變化。`,"Here are four kinds of algorithm working on 2 items. Each block is one step of work. They look much the same.":`這裡有四種演算法，各自處理 2 個項。每個方塊是一步工作。它們看起來差不多。`,"On small inputs almost anything is fast. The differences show when n grows.":`輸入很小的時候，幾乎什麼都快。n 變大時，差別才顯現出來。`,constant:`常數`,logarithmic:`對數`,linear:`線性`,quadratic:`平方`,"Steps for n = 2 items.":`n = 2 個項時的步數。`,"Double the input":`輸入翻倍`,"Give them 4 items instead of 2. One platform has not changed. One gained a single block. One doubled. One is four times the size.":`給它們 4 個項，而不是 2 個。一個平臺沒有變化。一個多了一個方塊。一個翻了一倍。一個變成了四倍大。`,"That reaction to growth is what Big-O describes.":`這種對增長的反應，正是大 O 所描述的。`,"Steps for n = 4 items.":`n = 4 個項時的步數。`,"Double it again":`再翻一倍`,"8 items. The same thing happens again, each growing in its own way: not at all, by one, by double, by four times.":`8 個項。同樣的事情再次發生，每個都按自己的方式增長：完全不變、多一步、翻倍、變成四倍。`,"Big-O names the <strong>shape of the growth</strong>, and ignores the details. 2n steps and n + 5 steps are both just O(n).":`大 O 說的是<strong>增長的形狀</strong>，忽略細節。2n 步和 n + 5 步都只是 O(n)。`,"“O(n)” is “the work grows in step with n.”":`「O(n)」的意思是「工作量隨 n 同步增長」。`,"Steps for n = 8 items.":`n = 8 個項時的步數。`,"O(1): constant":`O(1)：常數`,Constant:`常數`,"The work does not depend on n at all. Reading an array cell by its index, pushing onto a stack: one step, for 8 items or 8 million.":`工作量完全不取決於 n。按索引讀取陣列的一個格子、往堆疊裡壓入一個值：一步，不管是 8 個項還是 800 萬個。`,"This is as good as it gets.":`沒有比這更好的了。`,"O(log n): logarithmic":`O(log n)：對數`,Logarithmic:`對數`,"Each step throws away half of what is left, as binary search does. Doubling the input adds just <strong>one</strong> more step.":`每一步都扔掉剩下的一半，就像二分搜尋那樣。輸入翻倍，只多<strong>一</strong>步。`,"A million items take about 20 steps. A billion take about 30.":`一百萬個項大約需要 20 步。十億個大約需要 30 步。`,"O(n): linear":`O(n)：線性`,Linear:`線性`,"Every item is looked at once: adding up a list, or searching one that is not sorted. Twice the input, twice the work.":`每個項都看一次：把一個列表加起來，或者在沒排序的列表裡搜尋。輸入翻倍，工作量也翻倍。`,"Often this is the best possible, because you cannot skip items you have never seen.":`這往往已經是最好的了，因為你沒法跳過從沒看過的項。`,"O(n²): quadratic":`O(n²)：平方`,Quadratic:`平方`,"Every item is compared with every other: a loop inside a loop. Twice the input, <strong>four times</strong> the work.":`每個項都要和其他每個項比較：迴圈裡套迴圈。輸入翻倍，工作量變成<strong>四倍</strong>。`,"Fine for 8 items. For a million it is a trillion steps, and it is usually the first thing worth fixing.":`8 個項沒問題。一百萬個就是一萬億步，這通常是第一個值得最佳化的地方。`,"Much of this course is turning an O(n²) idea into O(n) or O(n log n).":`這門課的很多內容，就是把 O(n²) 的思路變成 O(n) 或 O(n log n)。`},memory:e,recursion:t,"divide-and-conquer":{"if problem is small enough:":`如果 問題足夠小:`,"return its answer directly       // base case":`返回 直接給出的答案       // 基本情況`,"split problem into smaller pieces    // divide":`把問題拆成更小的部分    // 分`,"solve each piece the same way        // conquer":`用同樣的方法解決每個部分        // 治`,"return their answers, put together   // combine":`返回 拼在一起的各部分答案   // 合`,"The shape of the work":`工作的形狀`,"Too big to do at once":`太大，沒法一次做完`,"Some problems are hard at full size and easy when they are tiny. Sorting eight cards takes thought. Sorting one card takes none.":`有些問題在完整規模時很難，變得很小時就很容易。給八張牌排序要動腦子，給一張牌排序完全不用。`,"<strong>Divide and conquer</strong> is a recipe for getting from the first to the second: split the problem, solve the pieces, and join their answers.":`<strong>分治</strong>是從前者走到後者的方法：拆分問題，解決各部分，再合併它們的答案。`,"a problem of size 8":`規模為 8 的問題`,"Pieces at the bottom":`底層的部分`,"Size of each":`每部分的大小`,Levels:`層數`,"Cut the problem into smaller problems of the same kind. Most often that means in half: two problems of size 4.":`把問題切成同類的更小問題。最常見的是對半切：兩個規模為 4 的問題。`,"Nothing has been solved yet. But each half can now be handled by the very same method, which is where recursion comes in.":`還什麼都沒解決。但現在每一半都可以用完全相同的方法處理，這就是遞迴登場的地方。`,"Until it is trivial":`直到變得微不足道`,"Each half is halved again, and again, until the pieces cannot get smaller. A piece of size 1 needs no work: that is the <strong>base case</strong>.":`每一半再對半切，一次又一次，直到不能再小。規模為 1 的部分不需要任何工作：這就是<strong>基本情況</strong>。`,"Halving 8 reaches 1 in three cuts. Halving n takes log n.":`8 對半切三次就到 1。n 對半切需要 log n 次。`,"Combine on the way back":`在返回的路上合併`,"Now the answers travel upward. Two solved pieces are joined into the answer for the piece above them, and so on to the top.":`現在答案向上傳遞。兩個已解決的部分合併成它們上一層部分的答案，一直到頂。`,"The numbers show the order pieces are finished in. Both halves are always done before the whole they belong to.":`數字表示各部分完成的順序。兩半總是在它們所屬的整體之前完成。`,"In merge sort, this joining is the merge.":`在合併排序裡，這個合併就是合併。`,"Add it up level by level":`一層一層地加起來`,"How much work is that? Look across each level. However the 8 is cut up, the sizes on one level still add up to 8.":`這一共要多少工作？橫著看每一層。不管 8 怎麼切，同一層的大小加起來仍然是 8。`,"If joining takes time in proportion to the size of the piece, as merging does, every level costs n. There are log n + 1 levels, so the total is about n log n.":`如果合併所需的時間與部分的大小成正比，就像合併那樣，那麼每層的代價是 n。一共有 log n + 1 層，所以總量大約是 n log n。`,"Depth 0":`深度 0`,"Depth 1":`深度 1`,"Depth 2":`深度 2`,"Depth 3":`深度 3`,Total:`總計`,"4 levels × 8 = 32":`4 層 × 8 = 32`,"Or follow only one branch":`或者只走一個分支`,Variation:`變體`,"Some methods split the problem and then need only <em>one</em> of the pieces. Binary search looks at the middle and throws the other half away.":`有些方法拆分問題後只需要其中<em>一個</em>部分。二分搜尋看一眼中間，就把另一半扔掉。`,"Then the work is one piece per level: log n in all. Counting pieces per level and work per piece is how every cost of this kind is found.":`那麼每層只有一個部分的工作量：總共 log n。數清每層有幾個部分、每個部分要多少工作，這類代價都是這樣算出來的。`,"Merge sort":`合併排序`,"both halves, n to join: n log n":`兩半都要，合併要 n：n log n`,"Binary search":`二分搜尋`,"one half, 1 to choose: log n":`只要一半，選擇要 1：log n`,"one part, n to split: about n":`只要一部分，拆分要 n：大約 n`,"When it fits":`什麼時候適用`,"It works when the pieces are <strong>independent</strong>: solving one tells you nothing about another. Merge sort, quick sort, binary search and quickselect are all this recipe.":`當各部分<strong>相互獨立</strong>時，它就適用：解決一個部分不會告訴你任何關於另一個部分的事。合併排序、快速排序、二分搜尋和快速選擇都是這個方法。`,"When the same small piece keeps turning up inside different big ones, solving it afresh each time is wasteful. That is the sign to switch to dynamic programming.":`如果同一個小部分在不同的大部分裡反覆出現，每次都重新解決它就是浪費。這就是該換成動態規劃的訊號。`,"The four strategies":`四種策略`,"Divide and conquer, greedy, backtracking and dynamic programming. Most algorithms in this course are one of them.":`分治、貪婪、回溯和動態規劃。這門課裡的大多數演算法都屬於其中之一。`},arrays:n,"dynamic-arrays":{"if size = capacity:":`如果 size = capacity:`,"make a new array, twice as big":`新建一個兩倍大的陣列`,"for each item:":`對每個 項:`,"move it across":`把它搬過去`,"let the old array go":`釋放舊陣列`,"Size and capacity":`大小與容量`,"A fixed number of cells":`固定數量的格子`,"An array is given its cells when it is made, and it cannot be given more later: the memory after it may already belong to something else.":`陣列在建立時得到它的格子，之後不能再多給：緊挨著它的記憶體可能已經屬於別的東西了。`,"This one has room for three. Two are in use. That is its <strong>size</strong> (2) and its <strong>capacity</strong> (3).":`這個陣列能放三個。用了兩個。這就是它的<strong>大小</strong>（2）和<strong>容量</strong>（3）。`,"How do lists that “just grow” work, if arrays cannot?":`既然陣列不能變大，那些「自己會長」的列表是怎麼做到的？`,"of 3":`/ 3`,"Appends so far":`已追加次數`,"Items moved":`已移動項數`,"Append, while there is room":`有空位時追加`,"Adding at the end is easy when a cell is free: put the value in the next one and count it.":`有空格子時，在末尾新增很容易：把值放進下一個格子，然後計數加一。`,"13 goes into cell 2. Nothing else has to move, so it is O(1). But now the array is full.":`13 放進格子 2。其他什麼都不用動，所以是 O(1)。但現在陣列滿了。`,"No room":`沒有空位`,"Now append 21. There is no cell 3: the array ends at cell 2, and it cannot be stretched.":`現在追加 21。沒有格子 3：陣列在格子 2 就結束了，而且不能拉長。`,"The value has nowhere to go.":`這個值無處可放。`,"Size equals capacity: time to grow.":`大小等於容量：該擴容了。`,"Make a bigger one":`造一個更大的`,"The way out is to ask for a whole new array, somewhere there <em>is</em> room.":`出路是申請一個全新的陣列，放在<em>有</em>空間的地方。`,"Not one cell bigger: <strong>twice as big</strong>. That choice is what makes this cheap, as you will see.":`不是隻大一格，而是<strong>大一倍</strong>。正是這個選擇讓它變得便宜，你馬上就會看到。`,"Why double":`為什麼翻倍`,"One extra cell would mean moving everything again on the very next append.":`只多一格的話，下一次追加就又得把所有東西搬一遍。`,"Move everything across":`全部搬過去`,"Every item is moved into the new array, one at a time, keeping its index.":`每一項都被搬進新陣列，一次一個，索引保持不變。`,"This is the expensive part: three items, three moves. With a million items it would be a million.":`這是昂貴的部分：三個項，三次移動。如果有一百萬個項，就是一百萬次。`,"A grow is O(n). It is the price of the append that triggered it.":`一次擴容是 O(n)。這是觸發它的那次追加付出的代價。`,"Swap, then append":`替換，然後追加`,"The old array is let go and the new one takes its place. To the rest of the program it is the same list: same items, same indexes.":`舊陣列被釋放，新陣列取代它的位置。對程式的其他部分來說，它還是同一個列表：同樣的項，同樣的索引。`,"And now there is a cell 3. 21 goes in.":`現在有格子 3 了。21 放進去。`,"Cheap again":`又便宜了`,"34 and 55 go straight in: the doubling bought three free cells. Then it is full again, and the next grow will make 12.":`34 和 55 直接放進去：翻倍換來了三個空格子。然後又滿了，下一次擴容會得到 12 格。`,"Each grow is twice as far away as the last. Spread over all the appends, the moving comes to about one extra step each: appending is O(1) <strong>on average</strong>. Averaging a cost over a whole run of operations like this is called <strong>amortized</strong> analysis.":`每次擴容都比上一次隔得遠一倍。把搬運分攤到所有追加上，每次大約只多一步：追加<strong>平均</strong>是 O(1)。像這樣把代價平攤到一整串操作上，叫作<strong>均攤</strong>分析。`,"This is the list in Python, the ArrayList in Java, the vector in C++.":`這就是 Python 的 list、Java 的 ArrayList、C++ 的 vector。`,"Six appends, three moves.":`六次追加，三次移動。`},"two-pointers":{"left ← 0, right ← last index":`left ← 0，right ← 最後一個索引`,"while left < right:":`當 left < right:`,"if sum = target: return left, right":`如果 sum = target: 返回 left, right`,"if sum < target: left ← left + 1":`如果 sum < target: left ← left + 1`,"else: right ← right − 1":`否則: right ← right − 1`,"How many looks":`看了幾次`,"A sorted row":`排好序的一排`,"Seven numbers, in order. Which two of them add up to <strong>14</strong>?":`七個數，按順序排列。哪兩個加起來等於 <strong>14</strong>？`,"You could try every pair, but there are 21 of them. Because the row is sorted, two markers can do it in a handful of looks.":`你可以試遍每一對，但一共有 21 對。因為這一排是排好序的，兩個標記看幾次就能解決。`,"Like binary search, this only works on sorted data.":`和二分搜尋一樣，這隻適用於排好序的資料。`,"Looks so far":`已看次數`,"Pairs there are":`總對數`,"Trying every pair is O(n²).":`試遍每一對是 O(n²)。`,"Start at both ends":`從兩端開始`,"Put <strong>left</strong> on the smallest value and <strong>right</strong> on the largest, and add them.":`把 <strong>left</strong> 放在最小的值上，<strong>right</strong> 放在最大的值上，把它們加起來。`,"1 + 15 = 16. That is more than 14.":`1 + 15 = 16。比 14 大。`,"15 is too big to pair with anything: even with the smallest value it overshoots.":`15 太大，和誰配對都不行：即使配上最小的值也超了。`,"1 + 15 = 16 · too big":`1 + 15 = 16 · 太大`,"Too big: step right in":`太大：right 往裡走`,"So 15 is out for good. Move <strong>right</strong> one place in, and add again.":`所以 15 永遠出局了。把 <strong>right</strong> 往裡移一格，再加一次。`,"1 + 12 = 13. Now it is less than 14.":`1 + 12 = 13。現在比 14 小。`,"1 is too small to pair with anything that is left.":`1 太小，和剩下的任何值配對都不夠。`,"1 + 12 = 13 · too small":`1 + 12 = 13 · 太小`,"Too small: step left in":`太小：left 往裡走`,"1 is out. Move <strong>left</strong> one place in.":`1 出局。把 <strong>left</strong> 往裡移一格。`,"4 + 12 = 16. Too big again, so it is right’s turn to move.":`4 + 12 = 16。又太大了，所以輪到 right 移動。`,"4 + 12 = 16 · too big":`4 + 12 = 16 · 太大`,"12 is out, and <strong>right</strong> steps in to 10.":`12 出局，<strong>right</strong> 往裡走到 10。`,"4 + 10 = 14. That is the pair, at indexes 1 and 4.":`4 + 10 = 14。就是這一對，索引是 1 和 4。`,"Had the two markers met without a match, there would be no such pair.":`如果兩個標記相遇時還沒找到，那就不存在這樣的一對。`,"Four looks, instead of up to 21.":`看了四次，而不是最多 21 次。`,"Every look ruled one value out for good, and a marker never moves back.":`每看一次就永久排除一個值，而且標記從不後退。`,"So there can be at most n looks before the markers meet: <strong>O(n)</strong>, against O(n²) for trying every pair.":`所以在兩個標記相遇之前，最多看 n 次：<strong>O(n)</strong>，而試遍每一對是 O(n²)。`,"The same two-ended squeeze reverses a list in place and checks for a palindrome.":`同樣的兩端夾逼法，也能原地反轉列表、檢查迴文。`},"sliding-window":{"sum ← total of the first k items":`sum ← 前 k 項的總和`,"for each step to the right:":`對每個 向右的一步:`,"sum ← sum − the item leaving":`sum ← sum − 離開的項`,"sum ← sum + the item entering":`sum ← sum + 進入的項`,"if sum > best: best ← sum":`如果 sum > best: best ← sum`,"Window sums":`視窗的和`,"Best run of three":`最好的連續三個`,"Seven numbers in a row. Which three <em>next to each other</em> add up to the most?":`一排七個數。哪三個<em>相鄰</em>的數加起來最大？`,"You could add up every run of three from scratch. But each run shares two of its numbers with the one before, so most of that adding is repeated.":`你可以把每組連續三個都從頭加一遍。但每組都和前一組共用兩個數，所以大部分加法都是重複的。`,"A window three cells wide, sliding along the row.":`一個三格寬的視窗，沿著這一排滑動。`,"Sums so far":`已算的和`,Best:`最好`,"The first window":`第一個視窗`,Start:`開始`,"Put the window over the first three values and add them up, the ordinary way.":`把視窗放在前三個值上，用普通的方法加起來。`,"4 + 2 + 7 = 13. That is the best so far, because it is the only one so far.":`4 + 2 + 7 = 13。這是目前最好的，因為目前只有它一個。`,"Slide, don’t start over":`滑動，不要重來`,"Move the window one cell right. One value leaves on the left and one enters on the right; the two in the middle were already counted.":`把視窗右移一格。左邊離開一個值，右邊進來一個值；中間兩個已經算過了。`,"So take the old sum, subtract what left and add what came in: 13 − 4 + 1 = 10.":`所以拿舊的和，減去離開的，加上進來的：13 − 4 + 1 = 10。`,"Two operations, however wide the window is.":`兩次運算，不管視窗有多寬。`,"Keep the best":`保留最好的`,"Slide again: 10 − 2 + 8 = 16.":`再滑一次：10 − 2 + 8 = 16。`,"That beats 13, so it becomes the best so far.":`比 13 大，所以它成為目前最好的。`,"To the end":`一直到底`,"Two more slides reach the end of the row: 12, then 17.":`再滑兩次就到這一排的末尾：12，然後是 17。`,"The best run of three is 8, 3, 6.":`最好的連續三個是 8、3、6。`,"Each value entered the window once and left it once. That is all the work there was: <strong>O(n)</strong>.":`每個值進視窗一次、出視窗一次。全部工作就這麼多：<strong>O(n)</strong>。`,"Adding every run from scratch would be O(n × k), and it gets worse the wider the window.":`每組都從頭加是 O(n × k)，視窗越寬越糟。`,"The same idea finds the longest stretch of text without a repeated letter. There the window grows and shrinks.":`同樣的思路可以找出最長的沒有重複字母的一段文字。那時視窗會變大也會變小。`,"Seven values, five windows, four slides.":`七個值，五個視窗，滑動四次。`},"prefix-sums":{"for each i from 1 to the last:":`對於 i 從 1 到最後一個:`,"if i = 0: return total[j]":`如果 i = 0: 返回 total[j]`,"return total[j] − total[i − 1]":`返回 total[j] − total[i − 1]`,"Check it":`驗證一下`,"Adding up a stretch":`把一段加起來`,"What do cells 1 to 4 add up to? Add them one at a time: 1 + 4 + 1 + 5 = 11.":`格子 1 到 4 加起來是多少？一個一個加：1 + 4 + 1 + 5 = 11。`,"That is fine once. But asked about a hundred different stretches, you would add the same numbers again and again.":`一次還好。但如果要問一百個不同的區段，你就會一遍又一遍地加同樣的數。`,"O(n) for every question: the longer the stretch, the more to add.":`每個問題都是 O(n)：區段越長，要加的越多。`,"Adding them up":`逐個相加`,"With the totals":`用累計和`,"Do the adding once, up front. Walk along the row keeping a <strong>running total</strong>, and write it down behind each value.":`先把加法一次做完。沿著這一排走，維護一個<strong>累計和</strong>，並把它寫在每個值的後面。`,"Each total is the one before it plus the value in front of it: 3, then 3 + 1 = 4, then 4 + 4 = 8, and so on.":`每個累計和都等於前一個累計和加上它前面的值：3，然後 3 + 1 = 4，然後 4 + 4 = 8，依此類推。`,"“Everything from the start up to here.”":`「從開頭到這裡的全部。」`,"Six additions, done once.":`六次加法，只做一次。`,"One subtraction":`一次減法`,"Now ask again: cells 1 to 4. Everything up to cell 4 is 14. Everything <em>before</em> cell 1 is 3.":`現在再問：格子 1 到 4。到格子 4 為止的全部是 14。格子 1 <em>之前</em>的全部是 3。`,"Take one from the other and what is left is exactly the stretch: 14 − 3 = 11.":`一個減去另一個，剩下的正好就是這一段：14 − 3 = 11。`,"The values themselves were not touched. Two totals did it.":`值本身完全沒動。兩個累計和就解決了。`,"Any stretch":`任意一段`,"Cells 3 to 5: the total up to cell 5 is 23, and before cell 3 it is 8.":`格子 3 到 5：到格子 5 的累計和是 23，格子 3 之前是 8。`,"23 − 8 = 15, however long the stretch is.":`23 − 8 = 15，不管這一段有多長。`,"O(1) for every question.":`每個問題都是 O(1)。`,"From the start":`從開頭開始`,"Cells 0 to 3 start at the very beginning, so there is nothing before them to take away.":`格子 0 到 3 從最開頭開始，所以前面沒有什麼要減的。`,"The answer is just the total up to cell 3: 9.":`答案就是到格子 3 的累計和：9。`,"Without this case you would look for a total before the first one.":`沒有這個情況，你就會去找第一個累計和之前的累計和。`,"One pass to build the totals, then every question is a single subtraction.":`一趟構建累計和，之後每個問題都只是一次減法。`,"It costs a second row of memory. And if a value changes, every total after it is wrong and has to be rebuilt.":`代價是多一排記憶體。而且如果某個值變了，它後面的每個累計和都錯了，必須重建。`,"Many questions about data that stays put: prefix sums. Data that keeps changing: something else.":`對不變的資料問很多問題：用字首和。資料一直在變：用別的方法。`,"Build: O(n), once. Ask: O(1), every time.":`構建：O(n)，一次。查詢：O(1)，每次。`},"maximum-subarray":{"best ← the first item":`best ← 第一項`,"if run > best: best ← run":`如果 run > best: best ← run`,"if run < 0: run ← 0     // a run in debt is dropped":`如果 run < 0: run ← 0     // 欠債的累計直接丟掉`,Totals:`累計`,"The best stretch":`最好的一段`,"Some of these numbers are gains and some are losses. Which unbroken stretch adds up to the most?":`這些數有的是收益，有的是虧損。哪一段連續的數加起來最大？`,"There are n² stretches to try. But one pass along the row is enough, if you carry the right two numbers with you.":`要試的區段有 n² 個。但只要隨身帶著對的兩個數，沿著這一排走一趟就夠了。`,"Current run":`當前累計`,"Best so far":`目前最好`,"Walk along the row adding each number to a <strong>run</strong>. After the first cell the run is 3, and that is also the best seen so far.":`沿著這一排走，把每個數加到一個<strong>累計</strong>上。過了第一個格子，累計是 3，這也是目前見過最好的。`,"Drop a run in debt":`丟掉欠債的累計`,"Adding −4 takes the run to −1. A run that has gone negative can only drag down whatever comes next.":`加上 −4，累計變成 −1。一個已經變成負數的累計，只會拖累後面的任何東西。`,"So forget it. The next cell starts a new run from nothing. The best so far is still 3.":`所以忘掉它。下一個格子從零開始新的累計。目前最好的仍然是 3。`,"The whole trick":`全部的訣竅`,"Anything that sums to less than zero is not worth carrying forward.":`任何加起來小於零的東西，都不值得帶著往前走。`,"run = −1: drop it":`run = −1：丟掉`,"Start afresh":`重新開始`,"5 begins a new run, and 5 beats the old best of 3.":`5 開始了新的累計，而 5 超過了舊的最好值 3。`,"A dip can be worth it":`下跌也可能值得`,"−2 lowers the run to 3. That is still positive, so it is kept. Then 4 lifts it to 7: a new best.":`−2 把累計降到 3。仍然是正數，所以保留。然後 4 把它抬到 7：新的最好值。`,"A small loss was worth sitting through for what came after it.":`為了後面的收穫，熬過一個小虧損是值得的。`,"−6 and 1 leave the run at 2, which never beats 7. The best stretch is 5, −2, 4.":`−6 和 1 讓累計停在 2，永遠超不過 7。最好的一段是 5、−2、4。`,"Every number was looked at once. This is Kadane’s algorithm, and it is dynamic programming in its smallest form: the best run ending here depends only on the best run ending one cell back.":`每個數都只看了一次。這就是 Kadane 演算法，它是最小形式的動態規劃：以這裡結尾的最好累計，只取決於以前一格結尾的最好累計。`,"O(n) time and two variables of memory.":`O(n) 時間，記憶體只要兩個變數。`,here:`這裡`},"merge-intervals":{"sort them by where they start":`按起點排序`,"run ← the first interval":`run ← 第一個區間`,"for each of the others:":`對每個 其餘的區間:`,"if it starts before run ends:":`如果 它在 run 結束之前開始:`,"stretch run to cover it":`拉長 run 來覆蓋它`,"keep run, and start a new one here":`保留 run，並在這裡開始新的一段`,"keep the last run":`保留最後一段`,"On the timeline":`在時間軸上`,"Overlapping stretches":`重疊的區段`,"Three bookings on a timeline. Each row is one booking; the blocks are the hours it covers. Some overlap.":`時間軸上有三個預訂。每一行是一個預訂；方塊是它佔用的小時。有些重疊了。`,"Combine any that overlap, so that what is left is a list of separate busy stretches. Calendars, memory allocators and genome tools all need this.":`把重疊的合併起來，剩下的就是一張互不相交的忙碌時段列表。日曆、記憶體分配器和基因組工具都需要這個。`,Intervals:`區間`,Merged:`合併後`,"Sort by start":`按起點排序`,"Put the intervals in order of where they begin. These already are: 0, 1, 6.":`把區間按開始的位置排好。這些已經排好了：0、1、6。`,"Sorted this way, anything that overlaps an interval must come straight after it. One pass will be enough.":`這樣排序後，任何與某個區間重疊的區間，一定緊跟在它後面。一趟就夠了。`,"Start a run":`開始一段`,"Begin the result with the first interval: a run from 0 to 2.":`用第一個區間開始結果：一段從 0 到 2。`,"It overlaps: stretch":`重疊了：拉長`,"B starts at 1. The run does not end until 2, so they overlap. Stretch the run to wherever B ends: 4.":`B 從 1 開始。這一段要到 2 才結束，所以它們重疊。把這一段拉長到 B 結束的地方：4。`,"Only two numbers were compared: B’s start and the run’s end.":`只比較了兩個數：B 的起點和這一段的終點。`,"starts inside the run":`在這一段內部開始`,"A gap: start again":`有空隙：重新開始`,"C starts at 6, after the run has ended at 4. There is a gap, so the run is finished. Keep it, and start a new one at C.":`C 從 6 開始，這時這一段已經在 4 結束了。有空隙，所以這一段完成了。保留它，從 C 開始新的一段。`,"starts after it ended":`在它結束之後開始`,"Two stretches":`兩個區段`,"Three bookings became two busy stretches. Each interval was looked at once, after sorting.":`三個預訂變成了兩個忙碌時段。排序之後，每個區間只看了一次。`,"Sorting first is what makes it easy. Without it, every interval would have to be checked against every other.":`先排序才讓它變得容易。不排序的話，每個區間都得和其他每個區間比一遍。`,"O(n log n) for the sort, then O(n) for the pass.":`排序 O(n log n)，然後一趟 O(n)。`},"pattern-matching":{"for each place the pattern could start:":`對每個 模式可能開始的位置:`,"compare it with the text, letter by letter":`把它和文字逐個字母比較`,"if every letter matches: return this place":`如果 每個字母都匹配: 返回 這個位置`,"Find one string in another":`在一個字串裡找另一個`,"A string is an array of characters. The commonest thing to ask of one is whether it contains another: is ABAC somewhere in ABABAC?":`字串是字元的陣列。對字串最常問的，就是它是否包含另一個字串：ABAC 在 ABABAC 裡嗎？`,"The text is the row behind. The pattern starts lined up with its beginning.":`文字是後面那一排。模式一開始和它的開頭對齊。`,"Letter by letter":`逐個字母`,"Compare the pattern with the text beneath it, left to right. A and A, B and B, A and A: three matches.":`從左到右，把模式和它下面的文字比較。A 和 A，B 和 B，A 和 A：三個匹配。`,"A mismatch":`不匹配`,"The fourth letter fails: the pattern wants C, and the text has B. The pattern is not here.":`第四個字母失敗了：模式要 C，文字是 B。模式不在這裡。`,"Slide along and start again":`往後滑，重新開始`,"The simple method moves the pattern one place to the right and begins again from its first letter. This time it fails at once: A against B.":`簡單的方法把模式右移一位，再從它的第一個字母開始。這次馬上就失敗了：A 對 B。`,"A match":`匹配`,"One more place along, and all four letters agree. The pattern is in the text, starting at index 2.":`再往後一位，四個字母全都一致。模式在文字裡，從索引 2 開始。`,"Do not look twice":`別看兩遍`,Faster:`更快`,"Nine comparisons, and some were wasted. When the first try failed, three letters had already matched, so the text there was known to be A B A. Starting at the next place could never have worked.":`九次比較，有些是浪費的。第一次嘗試失敗時，已經有三個字母匹配了，所以已知那裡的文字是 A B A。從下一個位置開始根本不可能成功。`,"Smarter methods use what has already matched to jump straight to the next place that could. The best known, KMP, never moves backwards in the text.":`更聰明的方法利用已經匹配的部分，直接跳到下一個可能成功的位置。最有名的 KMP，在文字裡從不回頭。`,"Slide-and-retry is O(n × m) at worst. KMP is O(n + m).":`逐位滑動重試最壞是 O(n × m)。KMP 是 O(n + m)。`,"a jump of 2 would do":`跳 2 格就行`,"With the jump: 8 comparisons.":`跳著走：8 次比較。`},kmp:r,matrices:i,"linked-lists":{"next → the node after it, or nothing":`next → 它後面的節點，或者空`,"repeat k times:":`重複 k 次:`,"return cur":`返回 cur`,"node ← a new node holding value":`node ← 一個存放 value 的新節點`,"A chain of nodes":`一串節點`,"A linked list keeps each value in its own <strong>node</strong>. Next to the value, the node stores a pointer to the node that comes after it.":`連結串列把每個值放在它自己的<strong>節點</strong>裡。在值的旁邊，節點存著一個指向下一個節點的指標。`,"The list itself only remembers where the first node is: the <strong>head</strong>. The last node points at nothing.":`連結串列本身只記得第一個節點在哪裡：也就是<strong>頭節點</strong>。最後一個節點什麼都不指向。`,"The beads show the order the list is read in: from the head, along one pointer after another.":`珠子表示讀取連結串列的順序：從頭節點開始，沿著一個又一個指標走。`,"A treasure hunt. Each clue tells you where to find the next one.":`尋寶遊戲。每條線索都告訴你下一條在哪裡。`,"Follow the pointers":`沿著指標走`,Traversal:`遍歷`,"Nodes have no index numbers. To reach the third one you start at the head and hop along the pointers, one node at a time.":`節點沒有索引。要到達第三個節點，你得從頭節點出發，沿著指標一次跳一個節點。`,"Look at the table: the nodes are not even next to each other in memory. Only the pointers put them in order.":`看看這張表：這些節點在記憶體中甚至不是挨著的。只有指標讓它們有了順序。`,"Reaching item k takes k hops: O(n). An array jumps straight there.":`到達第 k 項需要跳 k 次：O(n)。陣列可以直接跳過去。`,"A new node":`一個新節點`,"Insert · 1 of 3":`插入 · 第 1 步，共 3 步`,"Let’s add <strong>33</strong> after 27. First make a node for it.":`我們在 27 後面加入 <strong>33</strong>。先為它造一個節點。`,"It can live anywhere in memory. Nothing points at it yet, so it is not part of the list: it hangs off to one side, and the beads go straight past.":`它可以放在記憶體的任何地方。還沒有東西指向它，所以它還不是連結串列的一部分：它懸在一邊，珠子直接從旁邊經過。`,"Nobody had to make room for it. The other nodes stay exactly where they are.":`沒有誰需要為它騰地方。其他節點都待在原地不動。`,"Point it forward":`讓它指向前方`,"Insert · 2 of 3":`插入 · 第 2 步，共 3 步`,"Copy 27’s pointer into the new node, so that 33 points at 45.":`把 27 的指標複製到新節點裡，這樣 33 就指向 45。`,"The list still runs 12 → 27 → 45. Nothing is broken, and nothing can see 33 yet.":`連結串列仍然是 12 → 27 → 45。什麼都沒壞，也還沒有誰能看到 33。`,"Order matters":`順序很重要`,"Do this first. Re-point 27 first and you lose the only way to reach 45.":`先做這一步。如果先改 27 的指標，你就失去了到達 45 的唯一途徑。`,"Re-link":`重新連線`,"Insert · 3 of 3":`插入 · 第 3 步，共 3 步`,"Now point 27 at the new node. 33 is part of the list, so it takes its place in line: 12 → 27 → 33 → 45.":`現在讓 27 指向新節點。33 成了連結串列的一部分，於是在佇列中就位：12 → 27 → 33 → 45。`,"The drawing makes room for it, but look at the table: no node changed address. Two pointer writes did it all. An array would have had to move 45 in memory.":`圖上為它騰出了位置，但看看這張表：沒有一個節點改變地址。兩次指標寫入就完成了一切。陣列的話就得在記憶體中移動 45。`,"O(1) once you are standing at the spot.":`只要你已經站在那個位置，就是 O(1)。`,"Delete by bypass":`繞過即刪除`,Delete:`刪除`,"To remove 27, point the node before it straight past it: 12 now points at 33.":`要刪除 27，就讓它前面的節點直接越過它：12 現在指向 33。`,"27 still points at 33, but nothing points at 27. It drops out of the line, and the list closes up without it.":`27 仍然指向 33，但沒有東西指向 27 了。它掉出了佇列，連結串列在沒有它的情況下重新接上。`,"One pointer write: O(1), again once you are at the spot.":`一次指標寫入：O(1)，同樣前提是你已經在那個位置。`,"The unreachable node drifts off to be cleaned up, and the list is 12 → 33 → 45.":`無法到達的節點飄走，等著被清理，連結串列變成 12 → 33 → 45。`,"Linked lists make adding and removing cheap. They pay for it with slow lookups and one extra pointer per item.":`連結串列讓新增和刪除變得便宜。代價是查詢慢，以及每項多一個指標。`,"Lots of inserting and removing in the middle: linked list. Lots of “give me item k”: array.":`經常在中間插入和刪除：用連結串列。經常「給我第 k 項」：用陣列。`},"doubly-linked-lists":{"visit cur":`訪問 cur`,"make a node n holding x":`新建一個存放 x 的節點 n`,"Singly or doubly":`單向還是雙向`,"A pointer each way":`每個方向一個指標`,"A singly linked node knows only what comes after it. A <strong>doubly linked</strong> node keeps a second pointer, <em>prev</em>, to the node before.":`單向連結串列的節點只知道它後面是什麼。<strong>雙向連結串列</strong>的節點還存著第二個指標 <em>prev</em>，指向前一個節點。`,"The list also remembers both ends: <em>head</em> and <em>tail</em>. Now it can be read in either direction.":`連結串列也記住兩端：<em>head</em> 和 <em>tail</em>。現在兩個方向都能讀了。`,"A train where every carriage is coupled to the one in front and the one behind.":`一列火車，每節車廂都和前一節、後一節掛在一起。`,"Walk backwards":`反向遍歷`,cannot:`不能`,can:`能`,"Remove a node you hold":`刪除手上的節點`,"Add or remove at the tail":`在尾部新增或刪除`,"Pointers in every node":`每個節點的指標數`,"Left: singly linked. Right: doubly linked.":`左：單向連結串列。右：雙向連結串列。`,"Walk it backwards":`反向遍歷`,"Start at the tail and follow the prev pointers: 27, then 20, then 12.":`從 tail 開始，沿著 prev 指標走：27，然後 20，然後 12。`,"A singly linked list cannot do this at all. Its pointers only lead one way.":`單向連結串列完全做不到這一點。它的指標只通向一個方向。`,"Holding a node":`手上拿著一個節點`,"Suppose you already have hold of 20, and want it out of the list.":`假設你已經拿到了 20，想把它從連結串列裡拿掉。`,"With one pointer per node you would be stuck: removing it means changing the node <em>before</em> it, and the only way to find that is to walk from the head.":`如果每個節點只有一個指標，你就卡住了：刪除它意味著要修改它<em>前面</em>的節點，而找到那個節點的唯一方法是從頭節點走過去。`,"Unhook it both sides":`從兩邊解開它`,"Here 20 knows both its neighbours. Tell the one before to skip ahead, and the one after to skip back: two pointers rewritten, no walking.":`這裡 20 知道它的兩個鄰居。告訴前一個節點往前跳過它，告訴後一個節點往回跳過它：改寫兩個指標，不用遍歷。`,"Nothing points at 20 any more, so it is out of the list, and the list closes up.":`不再有東西指向 20，所以它離開了連結串列，連結串列重新接上。`,"O(1), wherever the node is. At either end, head or tail moves instead.":`O(1)，不管節點在哪裡。在兩端的話，改為移動 head 或 tail。`,"Add at the tail":`在尾部新增`,"The tail pointer makes the far end as easy to reach as the near one. To add 33, hook it to the old tail both ways and move tail along.":`有了 tail 指標，遠端和近端一樣容易到達。要新增 33，就把它和舊的尾節點雙向連起來，再把 tail 移過去。`,"Removing the last node is just as quick, because the tail knows what is before it.":`刪除最後一個節點也一樣快，因為尾節點知道它前面是誰。`,"None of this is free. Every node carries a second pointer, and every change has more pointers to keep right: miss one and the list reads differently forwards and backwards.":`這些都不是免費的。每個節點都多帶一個指標，每次修改都有更多指標要保持正確：漏掉一個，連結串列正著讀和反著讀就不一樣了。`,"Use one when you need to move both ways or remove from the middle: browser history, undo and redo, caches that drop the oldest entry.":`需要雙向移動或從中間刪除時就用它：瀏覽器歷史、撤銷和重做、丟棄最舊條目的快取。`,"Singly linked when you only ever go forwards. Doubly linked when you do not.":`只往前走就用單向連結串列。不是的話就用雙向連結串列。`},"fast-slow":{"while fast can make two more hops:":`當 fast 還能再跳兩次:`,"return slow":`返回 slow`,"if slow = fast: return yes":`如果 slow = fast: 返回 是`,"return no                // fast ran off the end":`返回 否                // fast 跑到了盡頭`,"The two cursors":`兩個遊標`,"Two cursors, two speeds":`兩個遊標，兩種速度`,"A linked list has no indexes and does not know its own length. To find its middle you could walk it once to count, then again to the halfway point.":`連結串列沒有索引，也不知道自己的長度。要找到中間，你可以先走一遍數個數，再走到一半的位置。`,"Or send <strong>two cursors</strong> down it together: <em>slow</em> takes one hop at a time, <em>fast</em> takes two.":`或者讓<strong>兩個遊標</strong>一起走：<em>slow</em> 一次跳一步，<em>fast</em> 一次跳兩步。`,"Also known as":`又稱`,"The tortoise and the hare.":`龜兔賽跑。`,"slow is on":`slow 在`,"0 hops":`跳 0 次`,"fast is on":`fast 在`,"Both start at the head.":`兩個都從頭節點開始。`,"One round":`一輪`,"In each round slow follows one pointer and fast follows two.":`每一輪 slow 沿一個指標走，fast 沿兩個指標走。`,"After one round slow is on 8 and fast is on 12. Fast is always twice as far from the head as slow.":`一輪之後 slow 在 8，fast 在 12。fast 離頭節點的距離總是 slow 的兩倍。`,"1 hop":`跳 1 次`,"2 hops":`跳 2 次`,"The middle":`中間`,"Another round, and fast is on the last node: it cannot make two more hops, so the walk stops.":`再走一輪，fast 到了最後一個節點：它不能再跳兩次了，所以停下。`,"Fast has covered the whole list. Slow has covered half of it, so slow is standing on the <strong>middle</strong>.":`fast 走完了整個連結串列。slow 走了一半，所以 slow 正站在<strong>中間</strong>。`,"One pass, no counting, and only two cursors of extra memory.":`一趟，不用計數，額外的記憶體只有兩個遊標。`,"4 hops":`跳 4 次`,"Fast went twice as far.":`fast 走了兩倍遠。`,"A list with a loop":`帶環的連結串列`,"Now a bug: the last node points back into the list instead of at nothing. There is no end any more.":`現在出了個 bug：最後一個節點不是指向空，而是指回連結串列裡。再也沒有盡頭了。`,"Anything that walks this list “until null” will go round for ever. How can a program tell, without remembering every node it has seen?":`任何「一直走到 null」的遍歷都會永遠繞圈。程式怎樣才能發現這一點，而不用記住見過的每個節點？`,"Back at the head, ready to try.":`回到頭節點，準備嘗試。`,"Send them round":`讓它們繞圈`,"Use the same two cursors. After two rounds slow is on 12 and fast is on 27, just as before.":`用同樣的兩個遊標。兩輪之後 slow 在 12，fast 在 27，和之前一樣。`,"Last time the walk ended here. This time fast still has somewhere to go.":`上次遍歷在這裡就結束了。這次 fast 還有地方可去。`,"Fast comes up behind":`fast 從後面追上來`,"Fast follows the pointer round the back and lands on 12, where slow has just left: slow is one node ahead, on 20.":`fast 沿著指標繞到後面，落在 12 上，而 slow 剛剛離開那裡：slow 領先一個節點，在 20 上。`,"Inside a loop there is no “ahead” for long. Each round fast gains one node on slow.":`在環裡，「領先」維持不了多久。每一輪 fast 都比 slow 多追上一個節點。`,"3 hops":`跳 3 次`,"6 hops":`跳 6 次`,"Fast is one node behind slow.":`fast 落後 slow 一個節點。`,"They meet":`它們相遇了`,"One more round and they are on the same node. Two cursors moving forward at different speeds can only meet if the list bends back on itself: <strong>there is a loop</strong>.":`再走一輪，它們就在同一個節點上了。兩個以不同速度前進的遊標，只有在連結串列繞回自身時才會相遇：<strong>有環</strong>。`,"If there were none, fast would simply have reached the end, as it did before.":`如果沒有環，fast 就會像之前那樣直接走到盡頭。`,"O(n) time and no extra memory. Remembering every visited node would cost O(n) memory.":`O(n) 時間，不用額外記憶體。記住每個訪問過的節點要花 O(n) 記憶體。`,"they meet: a loop":`相遇了：有環`,"8 hops":`跳 8 次`,"Same node: the list has a loop.":`同一個節點：連結串列有環。`},"reversing-a-list":{"prev ← nothing":`prev ← 空`,"next ← cur.next      // remember the rest":`next ← cur.next      // 記住剩下的部分`,"cur.next ← prev      // turn the pointer round":`cur.next ← prev      // 把指標掉頭`,"prev ← cur           // step along":`prev ← cur           // 往前走一步`,"return prev              // the new head":`返回 prev              // 新的頭節點`,"Two halves":`兩半`,"Turn every pointer round":`把每個指標都掉頭`,"This list reads 12, 20, 27, 33. Reverse it, so it reads 33, 27, 20, 12.":`這個連結串列讀作 12、20、27、33。把它反轉，讓它讀作 33、27、20、12。`,"With an array you would swap values. With a linked list the nodes can stay exactly where they are: only the <strong>pointers</strong> need to turn round.":`用陣列的話你會交換值。用連結串列的話，節點可以原地不動：只有<strong>指標</strong>需要掉頭。`,"Turned round":`已掉頭`,"Still to do":`還沒處理`,"Three cursors":`三個遊標`,"Turning 12’s pointer round would cut off the rest of the list, so first take hold of it: <em>next</em> remembers the node after <em>cur</em>.":`把 12 的指標掉頭會切斷連結串列剩下的部分，所以先抓住它：<em>next</em> 記住 <em>cur</em> 後面的節點。`,"<em>prev</em> is what cur should point at instead. For the first node that is nothing at all: it will be the new end.":`<em>prev</em> 是 cur 應該改為指向的東西。對第一個節點來說，那就是空：它會成為新的末尾。`,"Forget to save next and the rest of the list is unreachable the moment you rewrite the pointer.":`忘了儲存 next，在你改寫指標的那一刻，連結串列剩下的部分就再也到不了了。`,"Turn the pointer":`把指標掉頭`,Rewrite:`改寫`,"Now it is safe. <strong>cur.next ← prev</strong>: 12 stops pointing at 20 and points back at nothing.":`現在安全了。<strong>cur.next ← prev</strong>：12 不再指向 20，而是指回空。`,"The list is in two pieces for the moment, and the cursors are holding one end of each.":`連結串列暫時分成了兩段，遊標各抓著一段的一頭。`,"Step along":`往前走一步`,Advance:`前進`,"All three cursors move one node on: prev takes cur’s place, cur takes next’s, and next looks one further.":`三個遊標都往前移一個節點：prev 佔據 cur 的位置，cur 佔據 next 的位置，next 再往前看一個。`,"Everything behind cur is already reversed. Everything from cur onwards is untouched.":`cur 後面的部分都已經反轉了。從 cur 往後的部分還沒動過。`,"The same two moves. 20’s pointer swings back to 12, then the cursors step along.":`同樣的兩個動作。20 的指標轉回指向 12，然後遊標往前走。`,"One node joins the reversed part each time.":`每次都有一個節點加入已反轉的部分。`,"27 now points back at 20. Looking ahead, next finds nothing after 33: one node to go.":`27 現在指回 20。往前看，next 發現 33 後面什麼都沒有：還剩一個節點。`,"Off the end":`走出盡頭`,"33 turns to point at 27, and cur steps off the end of the list. There is nothing left to turn round, so the loop stops.":`33 轉為指向 27，cur 走出了連結串列的盡頭。沒有需要掉頭的了，迴圈停止。`,"prev is standing on 33: the last node that was handled.":`prev 站在 33 上：最後處理的那個節點。`,"A new head":`新的頭節點`,"One thing is still wrong: head points at 12, which is now the end. Move it to where prev is.":`還有一處不對：head 指向 12，而它現在是末尾。把它移到 prev 所在的地方。`,"The list reads 33, 27, 20, 12. No node moved and none was copied: one pass, and three cursors of extra memory.":`連結串列讀作 33、27、20、12。沒有節點移動，也沒有節點被複制：一趟，額外記憶體只有三個遊標。`,"O(n) time, O(1) extra space.":`O(n) 時間，O(1) 額外空間。`,"Reversed in place.":`原地反轉完成。`},"merge-sorted-lists":{"tail ← a dummy node before the result":`tail ← 結果前面的一個啞節點`,"while both lists have nodes:":`當 兩個連結串列都還有節點:`,"take whichever front node is smaller":`取兩個隊首節點中較小的那個`,"tail.next ← that node":`tail.next ← 那個節點`,"tail ← that node":`tail ← 那個節點`,"tail.next ← whatever list is left":`tail.next ← 剩下的那個連結串列`,"return the node after the dummy":`返回 啞節點後面的節點`,"The merge":`合併`,"Two lists into one":`兩個連結串列合成一個`,"Two linked lists, each already in order: 1, 4, 6 in front and 2, 3, 5 behind. Combine them into one sorted list.":`兩個連結串列，各自已經有序：前面是 1、4、6，後面是 2、3、5。把它們合併成一個有序連結串列。`,"With arrays this needs a third array to copy into. With linked lists, no node is copied or moved in memory. Only pointers change.":`用陣列的話，需要第三個陣列來複制。用連結串列的話，沒有節點在記憶體中被複制或移動。只有指標會變。`,"Merged so far":`已合併`,"Front of list A":`連結串列 A 的隊首`,"Front of list B":`連結串列 B 的隊首`,"Compare the fronts":`比較隊首`,"Both lists are sorted, so the smallest node overall is at the front of one of them. 1 is smaller than 2: it becomes the head of the result.":`兩個連結串列都是有序的，所以全部節點中最小的一定在其中一個的隊首。1 比 2 小：它成為結果的頭節點。`,"Splice the smaller one in":`把較小的接進來`,"Now the fronts are 4 and 2. 2 is smaller, so it comes next: point 1 at 2, and 2 on to whatever follows.":`現在隊首是 4 和 2。2 更小，所以它是下一個：讓 1 指向 2，2 再指向後面跟著的東西。`,"Two pointers were rewritten. The node itself is the same node it always was.":`改寫了兩個指標。節點本身還是原來那個節點。`,"4 against 3: 3 is next. It goes in after 2.":`4 對 3：3 是下一個。它接在 2 後面。`,"Whichever is smaller":`哪個小取哪個`,"4 against 5: this time the node already in line wins, and nothing needs rewiring. Then 6 against 5: 5 goes in before 6.":`4 對 5：這次勝出的節點本來就在佇列裡，不需要重新連線。然後 6 對 5：5 插到 6 前面。`,"One list":`一個連結串列`,"When one list runs out, the rest of the other is already in order and already linked: attach it and stop.":`當一個連結串列用完時，另一個剩下的部分已經有序、已經連好了：接上去就結束。`,"Six nodes, one pass, and not one of them was copied. This is the merge step of merge sort, done on a linked list.":`六個節點，一趟，沒有一個被複制。這就是合併排序的合併步驟，只不過是在連結串列上做的。`,"O(n + m) time and O(1) extra space.":`O(n + m) 時間，O(1) 額外空間。`},"lru-cache":{"node ← map[key]          // straight to it":`node ← map[key]          // 直接找到它`,"unhook node, put it at the front":`解開 node，把它放到最前面`,"return node.value":`返回 node.value`,"if the cache is full:":`如果 快取已滿:`,"remove the node at the back, and its key from the map":`刪除最後面的節點，並從 map 中刪除它的鍵`,"put a new node at the front":`在最前面放一個新節點`,"map[key] ← that node":`map[key] ← 那個節點`,"The cache":`快取`,"A cache with a limit":`有上限的快取`,"A cache keeps recent answers to hand so they need not be worked out again. It has limited room, so when it is full something must go. A good rule: throw out whatever was used <strong>least recently</strong>.":`快取把最近的答案放在手邊，省得再算一遍。它的空間有限，所以滿了的時候必須扔掉一些。一個好規則：扔掉<strong>最久沒用</strong>的那個。`,"This list holds three entries in order of use. The head is the newest, the tail the one that has gone longest untouched.":`這個連結串列按使用順序存著三個條目。頭部是最新的，尾部是最久沒碰過的。`,"In the map":`在 map 中`,"Recently used":`最近使用`,"newest first":`最新的在前`,Room:`空間`,"3 of 3":`3 / 3`,"Find it at once":`一下就找到`,Get:`獲取`,"Ask for A. Walking the list to find it would be O(n). So beside the list there is a <strong>hash map</strong> from each key to its node, and the map goes straight there.":`請求 A。遍歷連結串列去找它是 O(n)。所以連結串列旁邊有一個<strong>雜湊表</strong>，從每個鍵對映到它的節點，雜湊表直接就能找到。`,"The map points at A’s node.":`map 指向 A 的節點。`,"Unhook it":`解開它`,"A has just been used, so it is no longer the oldest. Take it out of its place: because the list is doubly linked, that is two pointer changes, with no searching.":`A 剛剛被用過，所以它不再是最舊的了。把它從原來的位置拿出來：因為連結串列是雙向的，只需改兩個指標，不用搜尋。`,"To the front":`放到最前面`,"Put it back at the head. The list is in order of use again, and B is now the one at risk.":`把它放回頭部。連結串列又是按使用順序排列的了，現在面臨淘汰的是 B。`,"Full: evict the oldest":`滿了：淘汰最舊的`,"Now store D. There is no room, so the least recently used entry goes: whatever is at the tail. That is B. Its key is removed from the map too.":`現在存入 D。沒有空間了，所以最久沒用的條目要走：也就是尾部的那個。那是 B。它的鍵也從 map 中刪除。`,"2 of 3":`2 / 3`,"B has been evicted.":`B 已被淘汰。`,"Two structures, one job":`兩個結構，一份工作`,"D goes in at the head. Neither structure could do this alone: the map finds an entry instantly but has no order, and the list keeps the order but cannot find anything quickly.":`D 放進頭部。這兩個結構單獨都做不到：雜湊表能立刻找到條目，但沒有順序；連結串列保持順序，但什麼都找不快。`,"Together, every operation is a lookup and a few pointer changes.":`合在一起，每個操作都只是一次查詢加幾次指標修改。`,"O(1) for get and for put, however big the cache is.":`不管快取多大，get 和 put 都是 O(1)。`},stacks:a,"balanced-brackets":{"for each character c:":`對每個 字元 c:`,"if c opens a bracket: push it":`如果 c 是開括號: 把它壓入堆疊`,"if c closes one:":`如果 c 是閉括號:`,"if the stack is empty: return no":`如果 堆疊為空: 返回 否`,"if the top does not match c: return no":`如果 堆疊頂與 c 不配對: 返回 否`,pop:`彈出`,"return whether the stack is empty":`返回 堆疊是否為空`,"Reading along":`逐個讀取`,"Does every bracket close?":`每個括號都閉合了嗎？`,"Is ( [ ] ) balanced? Every opener needs a closer of the same kind, and they must close in the reverse of the order they opened.":`( [ ] ) 是匹配的嗎？每個開括號都需要一個同類的閉括號，而且閉合的順序必須和開啟的順序相反。`,"“Most recent first” is exactly what a stack does. Read the text left to right; the first character is waiting.":`「最近的優先」正是堆疊做的事。從左到右讀文字；第一個字元在等待。`,"Characters read":`已讀字元`,"Openers go on the stack":`開括號進堆疊`,"( opens a bracket. Nothing can be checked yet, so push it and move on. It will wait there until its closer turns up.":`( 是開括號。現在還沒什麼可檢查的，所以把它壓入堆疊，繼續往下。它會一直在那裡等，直到它的閉括號出現。`,"The newest waits on top":`最新的在頂上等`,"[ opens another. Push it. The stack now holds the brackets still open, with the most recent on top.":`[ 又是一個開括號。壓入堆疊。現在堆疊裡存著還沒閉合的括號，最近的在頂上。`,"A closer checks the top":`閉括號檢查堆疊頂`,"] closes a bracket. The one it must close is whichever opened last: the top of the stack. That is [, the same kind. Pop it.":`] 是閉括號。它必須閉合的，是最後開啟的那個：堆疊頂。那是 [，同一類。彈出它。`,"[ ] match":`[ ] 配對`,"Empty at the end":`最後堆疊為空`,") closes (, which is now on top. Pop it. The text is finished and the stack is empty: every bracket found its partner.":`) 閉合 (，它現在在堆疊頂。彈出它。文字讀完了，堆疊也空了：每個括號都找到了自己的另一半。`,"One pass, one stack.":`一趟，一個堆疊。`,"O(n) time. The stack is never bigger than the deepest nesting.":`O(n) 時間。堆疊的大小不會超過最深的巢狀層數。`,"( ) match":`( ) 配對`,"Balanced.":`匹配。`,"Three ways to fail":`三種失敗`,"Take ( ] instead. The closer ] looks at the top and finds (, the wrong kind: not balanced.":`換成 ( ]。閉括號 ] 看向堆疊頂，發現是 (，型別不對：不匹配。`,"The other two failures: a closer arrives when the stack is empty, or the text ends with something still on the stack.":`另外兩種失敗：閉括號到來時堆疊是空的，或者文字結束時堆疊裡還有東西。`,"Compilers, code editors, and anything that reads nested text such as HTML or JSON.":`編譯器、程式碼編輯器，以及任何讀取 HTML、JSON 這類巢狀文字的東西。`,"] cannot close (":`] 不能閉合 (`,"Not balanced.":`不匹配。`},queues:o,"circular-buffer":{"if size = capacity: error":`如果 size = capacity: 錯誤`,"if size = 0: error":`如果 size = 0: 錯誤`,"return x":`返回 x`,"The buffer":`緩衝區`,"A queue in an array":`陣列裡的佇列`,"A queue adds at one end and removes at the other. In a plain array, removing from the front means shuffling everything else down: O(n) each time.":`佇列在一端新增、在另一端移除。在普通陣列裡，從前面移除意味著把其他所有東西往前挪：每次都是 O(n)。`,"A <strong>circular buffer</strong> never shuffles. It keeps two indexes instead: <em>head</em>, where the next item leaves, and <em>tail</em>, where the next one goes in.":`<strong>環形緩衝區</strong>從不挪動。它改為記住兩個索引：<em>head</em>，下一個項從這裡離開；<em>tail</em>，下一個項從這裡進入。`,"In the queue":`在佇列中`,"Enqueue: write at tail":`入隊：寫在 tail`,"Each new item is written at tail, and tail moves one cell along. Four items in: tail is at 4.":`每個新項都寫在 tail 處，然後 tail 往前移一格。進了四個項：tail 在 4。`,"Dequeue: read at head":`出隊：從 head 讀`,"To remove, read the item at head and move head along. A and B leave. Nothing else moved: the queue just starts further in now.":`要移除，就讀出 head 處的項，並把 head 往前移。A 和 B 離開了。其他什麼都沒動：佇列只是從更靠裡的地方開始了。`,"Cells 0 and 1 are free again.":`格子 0 和 1 又空出來了。`,"Off the end, back to the start":`走出末尾，回到開頭`,Wrap:`迴繞`,"Two more go in, at cells 4 and 5. Tail would now be 6, but there is no cell 6. It <strong>wraps round</strong> to 0.":`又進了兩個，在格子 4 和 5。tail 現在應該是 6，但沒有格子 6。它<strong>迴繞</strong>到 0。`,"That is the “mod capacity” in the code, and it is the whole idea: the end of the array is joined to its beginning.":`這就是程式碼裡的「mod capacity」，也是整個思路所在：陣列的末尾和開頭連在一起。`,"Reusing the space":`重複利用空間`,"G goes into cell 0, the space A left behind. In the array it looks out of order. Read from head, wrapping at the end, it is exactly right: C, D, E, F, G.":`G 放進格子 0，也就是 A 留下的空位。在陣列裡它看起來順序是亂的。從 head 開始讀，到末尾就回繞，順序完全正確：C、D、E、F、G。`,"Round and round":`一圈又一圈`,"C and D leave, and head moves on to 4. The live part of the queue now runs off the end of the array and back in at the start.":`C 和 D 離開，head 移到 4。佇列中有效的部分現在跨過陣列的末尾，又從開頭接回來。`,"Nothing was ever shifted, and no memory was asked for after the start.":`從來沒有挪動過任何東西，開始之後也沒有再申請過記憶體。`,"O(1) for both operations, in a fixed block of memory. Used for audio, network packets and keyboard input.":`兩種操作都是 O(1)，用的是一塊固定的記憶體。用於音訊、網路資料包和鍵盤輸入。`},deques:s,"monotonic-stack":{"while the stack has a top smaller than x:":`當 堆疊頂比 x 小:`,"pop it: its answer is x":`彈出它：它的答案是 x`,"push x":`把 x 壓入堆疊`,"whatever is left has no answer":`剩下的都沒有答案`,"Where it has got to":`進行到哪裡了`,"Next greater":`下一個更大的數`,"For every number in 5, 3, 2, 6, 4, 8, find the <strong>next greater</strong> one: the first bigger number that comes after it. For 5 that is 6. For 4 it is 8.":`對 5、3、2、6、4、8 中的每個數，找出<strong>下一個更大的數</strong>：在它後面出現的第一個比它大的數。5 的是 6。4 的是 8。`,"Checking each number against everything after it works, but that is O(n²). A stack does it in one pass.":`把每個數和它後面的所有數比較也行，但那是 O(n²)。用堆疊一趟就能完成。`,"Keep the numbers still waiting for an answer. A block here is as wide as its value is big.":`存放還在等答案的數。這裡每個方塊的寬度和它的值一樣大。`,Answered:`已回答`,"Wait on the stack":`在堆疊上等待`,"5 has seen nothing bigger yet, because it has seen nothing at all. It goes on the stack to wait.":`5 還沒見過更大的數，因為它什麼都還沒見過。它進堆疊等待。`,"The stack holds exactly the numbers that have no answer so far.":`堆疊裡存的正好是目前還沒有答案的數。`,"Smaller ones wait":`小的也等著`,"3 arrives. Is it the answer for 5? No, it is smaller. So 5 keeps waiting, and 3 starts waiting too, on top of it.":`3 來了。它是 5 的答案嗎？不是，它更小。所以 5 繼續等，3 也開始等，在 5 的上面。`,"Always in order":`始終有序`,Invariant:`不變數`,"2 is smaller again, so it waits as well. Look at the shape: every block is smaller than the one beneath it.":`2 又更小，所以它也等著。看看形狀：每個方塊都比它下面的小。`,"That is what <strong>monotonic</strong> means, and it is no accident. Anything that would break the order is dealt with before the new value goes on.":`這就是<strong>單調</strong>的意思，而且這不是巧合。任何會打亂順序的東西，都會在新值進堆疊之前處理掉。`,"The smallest waiting value is always on top, so it is the first one a new value should be compared with.":`等待中的最小值總在頂上，所以新值總是先和它比較。`,"A bigger one arrives":`來了個更大的`,"6 is bigger than the top, 2. So 6 is what 2 was waiting for: pop it, with its answer. The same goes for 3, and then for 5.":`6 比堆疊頂的 2 大。所以 6 就是 2 在等的數：彈出 2，帶著它的答案。3 也一樣，然後是 5。`,"Three answers from one arrival. Then 6 itself goes on the stack to wait.":`一次到達，得到三個答案。然後 6 自己進堆疊等待。`,"And a smaller one":`再來個小的`,"4 is smaller than 6, so nothing is answered. It waits on top, and the stack is in order again.":`4 比 6 小，所以沒有誰得到答案。它在頂上等著，堆疊又是有序的了。`,"Clear it again":`再清一次`,"8 is bigger than 4 and bigger than 6: both come off, both with the answer 8.":`8 比 4 大，也比 6 大：兩個都出堆疊，答案都是 8。`,"Then 8 waits. It is the last value, so nothing is coming to answer it.":`然後 8 等待。它是最後一個值，所以不會再有誰來回答它了。`,"Whatever is still on the stack at the end never met anything bigger. 8 has no next greater value.":`到最後還留在堆疊裡的，從沒遇到過更大的數。8 沒有下一個更大的數。`,"Every number was pushed once and popped once, however the pops were bunched together. That is 2n steps: <strong>O(n)</strong>.":`不管彈出是怎麼扎成一團的，每個數都只壓入一次、彈出一次。一共 2n 步：<strong>O(n)</strong>。`,"Days until a warmer day, the span of a stock price, the largest rectangle in a histogram.":`離下一個更暖和的日子還有幾天、股價的跨度、直方圖中最大的矩形。`,"8 → none":`8 → 無`,"Six values, six pushes, six pops.":`六個值，六次壓入，六次彈出。`},"monotonic-queue":{"for each x in a, at index i:":`對每個 a 中的 x，索引為 i:`,"while the back of the deque is smaller than x:":`當 雙端佇列的後端比 x 小:`,"pop it from the back      // it can never win now":`把它從後端彈出      // 它再也不可能勝出了`,"push x at the back":`把 x 壓入後端`,"if the front has left the window: pop it from the front":`如果 前端已經離開視窗: 把它從前端彈出`,"once the window is full: the front is its maximum":`一旦視窗滿了: 前端就是它的最大值`,Candidates:`候選`,"The biggest in every window":`每個視窗裡最大的`,"Slide a window of three along this row and report the largest value in it each time.":`讓一個三格的視窗沿著這一排滑動，每次報出其中最大的值。`,"Scanning each window afresh costs three looks per window. A deque that keeps only the values that could still win does it in one pass.":`每個視窗都重新掃描，每個視窗要看三次。用一個只保留還可能勝出的值的雙端佇列，一趟就能完成。`,Deque:`雙端佇列`,Maximums:`最大值`,"Keep the candidates":`保留候選`,"4 arrives: a candidate. 2 arrives. It is smaller than 4, but it is also newer, so it will outlast 4 in the window. It might be the maximum later. Keep both.":`4 來了：一個候選。2 來了。它比 4 小，但它也更新，所以它在視窗裡會比 4 待得久。它以後可能是最大值。兩個都留著。`,"smaller, but newer":`更小，但更新`,"Bigger and newer beats both":`又大又新，勝過兩者`,"5 arrives. It is bigger than 2 and bigger than 4, and it will be in the window longer than either. Neither can ever be the maximum again: throw them out.":`5 來了。它比 2 大，也比 4 大，而且它在視窗裡會比它們待得都久。它們倆再也不可能是最大值了：扔掉。`,"The window is full, and the front of the deque is its maximum: 5.":`視窗滿了，雙端佇列的前端就是它的最大值：5。`,"Why “monotonic”":`為什麼叫「單調」`,"What is left in the deque always runs from biggest to smallest.":`雙端佇列裡剩下的，總是從大到小排列。`,"max = 5":`最大值 = 5`,"The window moves on and 1 arrives. It beats nothing, so it queues up behind 5. The maximum is still the front: 5.":`視窗往前移，1 來了。它誰也勝不過，所以排在 5 後面。最大值仍然是前端：5。`,"Out of the back":`從後端出去`,"3 arrives and knocks out 1, which is smaller and older. 5 is still inside the window, and still the maximum.":`3 來了，把 1 擠了出去，1 更小也更舊。5 仍在視窗裡，仍是最大值。`,"6 arrives and clears the deque. 5 would have left anyway: the window has moved past it, and values that fall out of the window are dropped from the front.":`6 來了，清空了雙端佇列。5 反正也要走了：視窗已經越過了它，掉出視窗的值會從前端丟掉。`,"Every value entered the deque once and left it once.":`每個值都只進入雙端佇列一次、離開一次。`,"O(n) in total, whatever the window size.":`總共 O(n)，不管視窗多大。`,"max = 6":`最大值 = 6`}};export{n as arrays,c as default,s as deques,r as kmp,i as matrices,e as memory,o as queues,t as recursion,a as stacks};